# Pin line endings for the whole repo instead of relying on each contributor's own
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true
# disagrees with the LF-only files this repo stores, and every edited file shows as
# "modified" with a 0-byte diff, or every commit warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF" —
# pure line-ending noise. `eol=lf` matches what every source file already uses on disk.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF; everything else stays LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary formats — never touched by line-ending conversion. `text=auto` already
# autodetects these, but an explicit list survives a misdetection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
